From 9acf2bd17b969ee4c3c20f99ff388041ad2a9a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafa <2588276+rafatxf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:57:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] DFlash2: speculative (rejection) sampling for stochastic
 samplers

Upstream PR turboderp-org/exllamav3#423 by Rafa (@rafatxf), commit eef016b,
applied on top of the RDNA4 series (base 656b3f7). Rebased onto the batching series (rdna4-dev-batch) with one
adaptation: walk_sample now takes the path-aligned state and logits (path_state, logits). The batch series'
DFlash2 row pruning already slices them to block rows 1.. (and to the first dflash2_rows rows when the draft is
short), so the original state[:, 1:] / logits[:, 1:] would have sliced a second time. The doc section heading
and `import os` were already present on the new base.

With temperature > 0 the generator verified DFlash2's greedy selector path by sampling the target and accepting
matches, so a draft token was accepted with probability p(x). When the single active job's sampler is a stateless
distribution (temperature / top-k / top-p / min-p), the selector now samples its path from q = softmax(score / T_draft)
(CUDA: dflash2_selector_walk_sample, Gumbel-max, exports q) and the verifier accepts x with probability
min(1, p(x) / q(x)), resampling the first rejected position from normalize(max(p - q, 0)) and the bonus token from p
(Generator._spec_verify, one host sync per block). p is the job sampler's exact distribution (CustomSampler.probs: the
unfused step stack, with the full-vocabulary sort before a top-k replaced by topk). The output distribution is
unchanged (Monte Carlo test). T_draft = 0.5 T measured best (EXL3_DFLASH_SPEC_TSCALE).

Match-the-sample verification is kept for greedy jobs, other samplers (penalties, DRY, XTC, logit bias), jobs with
forced tokens or returned probabilities, drafters without a candidate selector (DFlash v1), and from the point where a
grammar filter becomes active inside a block (the block was resolved without filter masks). EXL3_DFLASH_SPEC=0
disables it.

tests/test_dflash_spec_sampling.py: the rejection-sampling verifier reproduces the target distribution (Monte Carlo).
tests/test_dflash2_walk_sample.py: the sampled selector walk draws from q and exports it.

GDN accepted-input replay (EXL3_GDN_REPLAY) needs no change: the resolved tokens go through the
same accept/reject loop, so the accepted length still reaches the recurrent state through
reject_remainder -> rewind(num_rejected), or rewind(0) on full acceptance.

